('03','Database, RLS, Storage and Canonical Documentation','PARTIAL','P0','Secure the data model before adding new relationships and content.','Migrations 002-004 and local 005 represent current security/lifecycle work; base schema and POLICIES.md contain historical definitions that must be clearly layered.','Verify remote/local state, add only additive migrations, document effective policies, add constraints/indexes/immutable fields, restrict SECURITY DEFINER/search_path/grants, and scope storage by actual object paths.','Preserve existing tables, lifecycle objects, room_messages compatibility, and working RLS. Never DROP TABLE, TRUNCATE, bulk-delete, replay 002/003, or create public bypasses.','Every new table needs FKs, unique/status constraints, indexes, ownership/member RLS, and rollback notes. Storage and cleanup remain lifecycle-aware.','RLS is authoritative; realtime publication/channel authorization must match it.','Unlocks social, rooms, groups, Music, and AI safely.','Migration dry run, schema diff, anonymous probes, full member-state matrix, storage path tests, direct server-action bypass tests.','Forward-compatible migrations and reversible policy/function changes.','Remote objects match intended policy state and private-data probes deny unauthorized access.'),
